<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" ?>
<!-- RPi profile: pin CycloneDDS to loopback PLUS whichever external link
     exists. Auto-select is unusable here: the eth-AP failover moves
     10.42.0.2 between eth0 and uap0, and a participant bound to the iface
     that just vanished keeps failing its socket writes forever (seen live:
     standalone boot bound to the wifi AP, cable plugged, AP torn down, every
     node spamming "ddsi_udp_conn_write failed" and the local pad pipeline
     dead, because discovery died with the iface).

     lo is required and always present, so the on-robot control loop
     (joy, teleop, policy, real_io, ros2_control) never depends on which
     external link is up. eth0/uap0 are best-effort: bound when present at
     stack start, giving the PC (cable) or phone/console (AP) a window in.
     A link flip mid-run still only degrades OUTSIDE visibility; restart the
     service (or re-dock) to rebind. Installed to /etc/cyclonedds-rpi.xml by
     install.sh; wojtek-robot.service and the ~/.bashrc env block point
     CYCLONEDDS_URI here.

     wlan0 is deliberately NOT listed: it is the upstream wifi station, and
     robot topics must not be multicast onto that foreign network. -->
<!-- 2026-09-27: the fleet lives on the venue wifi (the perception Pi and
     the DGX that runs the brain hand this robot its goals over DDS), so
     wlan0 (the wifi station) is bound too, with AllowMulticast=spdp:
     discovery may multicast, every topic flows unicast, nothing is
     multicast onto the venue network. Also: the Pi 4's radio cannot hold
     an AP and a station at once (brcmfmac leaves the station dead after
     the AP starts, -52 errors, see wojtek-net-switch.sh), so on a robot
     that lives on the venue wifi the AP switch is disabled:
         sudo systemctl disable wojtek-net; sudo systemctl stop wojtek-net
     (install.sh re-enables it on a provision). -->
<CycloneDDS xmlns="https://cdds.io/config" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="https://cdds.io/config https://raw.githubusercontent.com/eclipse-cyclonedds/cyclonedds/master/etc/cyclonedds.xsd">
    <Domain Id="any">
        <General>
            <AllowMulticast>spdp</AllowMulticast>
            <Interfaces>
                <NetworkInterface name="lo" multicast="true"/>
                <NetworkInterface name="eth0" presence_required="false"/>
                <NetworkInterface name="uap0" presence_required="false"/>
                <NetworkInterface name="wlan0" presence_required="false" multicast="true"/>
            </Interfaces>
        </General>
    </Domain>
</CycloneDDS>
